              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hot Chilli"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So good! I used whipped cream in place of the frozen whipped topping. Really easy to make and more than satisfied my Cookies 'n' Cream loving family. Thanks."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "karihelen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This cake was delicious, and quite simple to make. Just make sure to really crush the Oreos for the crust until the mass is as fine as possible, and use a bit more melted butter than the recipe suggests in order to make sure the crust stays together. I left the cake in the fridge for 24 hours, and the texture was perfect when I took it out. It looks good, too!",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-15T05:11:08.407Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ssr7mmrwps"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe and it was amazing and quick. I only made one change to the recipe which was golden oreos instead of the original and they were double stuff",
            "datePublished": "2022-08-08T00:32:05.961Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aki"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was easy and surprisingly good! I don't like Cool Whip, so I made real whipped cream.. I beat 1.5 cups cream, 1.5 tsp vanilla extract and sugar to taste",
            "datePublished": "2010-03-28T19:21:08.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "torian0319"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My kids and I were so excited to make this. I took a few if the suggestions that read: i used a 8 × 10 pyrex dish, 1/2 cup of butter instead of 1/4, reduced the amount of cream cheese from (4) 8 oz bars to 3, 1 cup of sugar, and I used 1 and 1/4 tub of cool whip. Even with these changes, it was still not sweet enough and the cream cheese overpowered the oreo cookie flavor. Next time, we will only use (2) 8 oz bars of cream cheese, two tubs of whip cream, 1 cup of sugar, and two packages of oreos. I think these adjustments will make this cheese perfect. But, it was still a decent recipe and a good base to tweak to your liking.",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-24T21:56:46.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ModestDove9231"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is so excellent and easy I make it constantly. My family absolutely devours it! It disappears at parties too! One of my favorite all-time recipes. Hint: once you've mixed the cookie crumbs with the butter and spread them out in the pan, spray the crumb mixture and your fingers with cooking spray and press down with your fingers. The crumbs won't stick to a spatula or your fingers at all and makes it so much easier.",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-27T23:02:50.908Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marcella"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very well-received by my company tonight. I don't know if I will make it again, but I might use this base recipe for other cookie-type no-bake desserts. I put it in an 8\" springform pan. The cheesecake, including the crust, was slightly less than 2 inches thick. I think it would be very thin if you spread it out in a 9 x 13 pan. I dressed it up with some chocolate covered strawberries that I made myself.",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-23T19:35:42.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "brisbois_c"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of the easiest and tastiest recipes I've ever tried! Took it with me to a party and it was the first cake to fnish :) I used freshly whipped cream instead of whipped topping, so that the amount of sugar can be reduced according to taste. Because it wasn't so sweet, the focus was on the oreos and cream cheese - delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2009-10-08T08:46:56.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amithyst Stonewall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for a friends birthday and it was great. If I made it again I'd probably reduce it to 3 blocks of the cream cheese though, it made a almost too much for my pie plate to handle!",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-23T01:04:47.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica Morrison"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is fantastic! The reviews I read about it having too much cream cheese are crazy. On the package of Philadelphia for making original cheese cake it says to use 4 pkg, and that's from the manufacturer. So if you don't like your cheesecake to taste like... cheesecake, don't use this recipe. But it was delicious. \n\nI didn't use the crust part of this, so I was able to use the whole pack or oreos in the cheesecake.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-26T09:26:02.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Keeli"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used all reduced fat cream cheese and fat free cool whip and this was still very rich. A small piece goes a long way, but I feel the crust should have been a bit thicker to help with serving. Very easy to make and everyone raved about it at the potluck.",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-09T04:48:28.447Z"
          },
